WEBVTT

00:00.730 --> 00:02.910
I've gotten feedback
that all the Chuck Norris

00:02.910 --> 00:05.326
imagery in the last video might
have been a little bit too

00:05.326 --> 00:06.140
overwhelming.

00:06.140 --> 00:08.640
So for this video, I've included
something a little bit more

00:08.640 --> 00:10.000
soothing.

00:10.000 --> 00:12.140
Let's try to simplify
some more expressions.

00:12.140 --> 00:13.860
And we'll see we're
just applying ideas

00:13.860 --> 00:15.730
that we already knew about.

00:15.730 --> 00:21.250
Let's say I want to simplify the
expression 2 times 3x plus 5.

00:21.250 --> 00:24.020
Well, this literally
means two 3x plus 5's.

00:24.020 --> 00:25.930
So this is the exact same thing.

00:25.930 --> 00:28.750
This is one 3x plus
5, and then to that,

00:28.750 --> 00:30.610
I'm going to add
another 3x plus 5.

00:30.610 --> 00:33.960
This is literally what
2 times 3x plus 5 means.

00:33.960 --> 00:37.330
Well, this is the same thing
as, if we just look at it right

00:37.330 --> 00:40.160
over here, we have now two 3x's.

00:40.160 --> 00:43.000
So we could write
it as 2 times 3x.

00:43.000 --> 00:52.490
Plus, we have two 5's,
so plus 2 times 5.

00:52.490 --> 00:55.360
You might say, hey, Sal, isn't
this just the distributive

00:55.360 --> 00:57.220
property that I know
from arithmetic?

00:57.220 --> 00:59.255
I've essentially just
distributed the 2?

00:59.255 --> 01:05.690
2 times 3x plus 2 times 5?

01:05.690 --> 01:08.102
And I would tell
you, yes, it is.

01:08.102 --> 01:10.560
And the whole reason why I'm
doing this is just to show you

01:10.560 --> 01:13.250
that it is exactly
what you already know.

01:13.250 --> 01:16.320
But with that out of the way,
let's continue to simplify it.

01:16.320 --> 01:21.430
When you multiply the 2
times the 3x, you get 6x.

01:21.430 --> 01:25.030
When you multiply the 2
times the 5, you get 10.

01:25.030 --> 01:28.364
So this simplified
to 6x plus 10.

01:28.364 --> 01:30.780
Now let's try something that's
a little bit more involved.

01:30.780 --> 01:34.710
Once again, really just
things that you already know.

01:34.710 --> 01:54.720
Let's say I had 7 times 3y minus
5 minus 2 times 10 plus 4y.

01:54.720 --> 01:57.410
Let's see if we
can simplify this.

01:57.410 --> 01:59.030
Well, let's work on
the left-hand side

01:59.030 --> 02:02.080
of the expression, the
7 times 3y minus 5.

02:02.080 --> 02:03.560
We just have to
distribute the 7.

02:03.560 --> 02:08.740
This is going to be 7 times 3y,
which is going to give us 21y.

02:08.740 --> 02:10.800
Or if I had 3 y's
7 times, that's

02:10.800 --> 02:13.770
going to be 21 y's, either way
you want to think about it.

02:13.770 --> 02:15.300
And then I have 7
times-- we've got

02:15.300 --> 02:19.100
to be careful with
the sign-- negative 5.

02:19.100 --> 02:22.640
7 times negative
5 is negative 35.

02:22.640 --> 02:24.180
So we've simplified
this part of it.

02:24.180 --> 02:26.610
Let's simplify the
right-hand side.

02:26.610 --> 02:29.690
You might be tempted to say,
oh, 2 times 10 and 2 times 4y

02:29.690 --> 02:30.990
and then subtract them.

02:30.990 --> 02:34.080
And if you do that right and
you distribute the subtraction,

02:34.080 --> 02:35.190
it would work out.

02:35.190 --> 02:39.357
But I like think of
this as negative 2,

02:39.357 --> 02:41.190
and we're going to
distribute the negative 2

02:41.190 --> 02:47.790
times 10 and the
negative 2 times 4y.

02:47.790 --> 02:53.870
So negative 2 times
10 is negative 20,

02:53.870 --> 02:56.660
so it's minus 20
right over here.

02:56.660 --> 03:00.130
And then negative 2 times
4, negative 2 times 4

03:00.130 --> 03:03.860
is negative 8, so it's
going to be negative 8y.

03:03.860 --> 03:06.760
Let's write a minus
8y right over here.

03:06.760 --> 03:08.586
And are we done simplifying?

03:08.586 --> 03:10.710
Well, no, there's a little
bit more that we can do.

03:10.710 --> 03:14.160
We can't add the 21y to the
negative 35 or the negative 20

03:14.160 --> 03:16.420
because these are
adding different things

03:16.420 --> 03:17.970
or subtracting different things.

03:17.970 --> 03:22.660
But we do have two things
that are multiplying y.

03:22.660 --> 03:24.620
Let me do all in
this green color.

03:24.620 --> 03:26.720
You have 21 y's right over here.

03:26.720 --> 03:33.730
And then we can view it as from
that we are subtracting 8 y's.

03:33.730 --> 03:37.540
So if I have 21 of something
and I take 8 of them away,

03:37.540 --> 03:39.270
I'm left with 13
of that something.

03:39.270 --> 03:42.190
So those are going to
simplify to 13 y's.

03:46.195 --> 03:48.310
I'll do this in a new color.

03:48.310 --> 03:52.270
And then I have
negative 35 minus 20.

03:52.270 --> 03:56.597
That's just going to
simplify to negative 55.

03:56.597 --> 03:58.680
So this whole thing
simplified, using a little bit

03:58.680 --> 04:00.810
of the distributive
property and combining

04:00.810 --> 04:06.072
similar or like terms,
we got to 13y minus 55.
